# Mozartbrunnen, St. Gilgen (1926): the young Mozart playing his violin on
# a limestone plinth. Statue: coat in verdigris t/T, face, hands, violin
# and breeches in bronze o/O/l, k outline (Taube sits on his head).
# Plinth x 16..31, rows 16..47 = exactly the upper two tiles of the 1-wide,
# 3-high solid plinth (D-038: its lit w cornice top is the collision top);
# the bottom tile (rows 48..63) is the basin row and stays the stone tile.
# Two bronze birds on the plinth spout light s/w/t jets into the basin -
# small, bright and light, never the dark hazard lake.
# idle: 2 frames, the jets' highlights and splashes move.
sprite = mozartbrunnen
size   = 48x64
origin = 24,64
anim   = idle frames=2 ticks=12 loop
